      "artist": "NPS",
      "description": "Paved pathway of the promenade\nWest side, Jackson Lake Lodge Promenade\nThe Jackson Lake Lodge Historic District is notable for its associations with the origins of the Mission 66 initiative and the adoption of modern architectural principles and forms by the NPS.  The geometric promenade and lawn of the main viewing terrace extend this formal modern design into the landscape.\nWhile this represents a break with the NPS Rustic-style design tradition, the landscape features suggest influences of both styles.\nKeywords: imr; grte; rustic style; mission 66; shoshone; jackson lake lodge; cultural landscape",
